# Real-word typo: "defiantly" (in open resistance) for "definitely". Common
# autocorrect slip; pattern from published lists; examples are ours.
# why: Definitely means certainly; defiantly means in open resistance. Autocorrect often swaps them, and the result can sound rude.
expr defiance [refuse, refused, refuses, refusing, reject, rejected, rejects, ignore, ignored, ignores, resist, resisted, resists, defy, defied, defies, stare, stared, stares, stand, stood, stands, raise, raised, raises, shout, shouted, shouts, march, marched, insist, insisted, insists, cross, crossed, lift, lifted, fold, folded, glare, glared, lean, leaned, jut, jutted, shake, shook, hold, held, keep, kept, remain, remained, continue, continued, sit, sat, walk, walked, toss, tossed, tilt, tilted, meet, met]
expr modal <([will, would, should, could, can, must, might, may, (we'll), (I'll), (you'll), (they'll), (he'll), (she'll), to, I, we, you, (we're), (I'm), (they're), have, has, had] defiantly !@defiance), defiantly>
expr main [@modal, <(defiantly [be, recommend, recommended, agree, worth, interested, going, coming, want, need, try, check, consider, help, the, a, an, one, more, better, worse, possible, true, right, (gonna), getting, happening, ready, sure, keen, confident, certain, positive, glad, happy, excited, thrilled, open, available, capable, qualified, able, planning, looking, love, buying, attending, joining, coming, interested, will, (would), (won't), (will), have, had, has, there, here, not, been, think, beat, order, address, finish, restart, attend, express, deducted, on, off]), defiantly>]

let message "Did you mean `definitely`? `Defiantly` means in open resistance."
let description "Catches `defiantly` where `definitely` was meant (I will defiantly be there)."
let kind "Typo"
let becomes "definitely"
let strategy "MatchCase"

test "I am defiantly confident in my skills." "I am definitely confident in my skills."
test "I will defiantly be there." "I will definitely be there."
test "This is defiantly worth a visit." "This is definitely worth a visit."
test "I'm defiantly interested in the role." "I'm definitely interested in the role."
test "We would defiantly recommend them." "We would definitely recommend them."
test "That was defiantly the best part." "That was definitely the best part."

allows "She defiantly refused to leave."
allows "He stared defiantly at the referee."
allows "The protesters stood defiantly in the rain."

test "The team will defiantly finish on time." "The team will definitely finish on time."
test "I have defiantly been putting it off." "I have definitely been putting it off."
test "I was defiantly not impressed." "I was definitely not impressed."
allows "She will defiantly refuse to comply."
allows "He was defiantly staring back."
